It generates the ALAC tests' audio with integer arithmetic only, so it is the same on every platform, and no recorded audio is in it. The ALAC files made from it live in tests/refs/alac: examples/record_refs encodes them with this crate's own ALAC writer (src/alac/refs.rs) and wraps them with its own MP4, QuickTime and Matroska writers (`cargo run --release --example record_refs -- alac`). src/alac/refs.rs lists every file with its channels, depth, rate, frames, the generator's salt, the hash of its PCM and the writer settings.
